
First we will test this code with controller 

Then use it with the main driver 

Keep in min -- Ak80  uses extended can id and feedback is in 298 id

The radar uses FMCW ie transmittion signal freq changes over time - 
    - beat frequency formed by delayed echo gives the range 
    - Doppler shift gives the velocity   -- ie you are getting relative speed
    So both are independently measured 
Radar gives a 4D point cloud 

Distance resolution is 0.1m   precesion is +-0.05m

Speed range +-18m/s   speed ratio 0.25m/s   precesion +- 0.12m/s

operation freq is 100ms 

Link to datasheet - https://robu.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/R164169-SR75-77GHz-Technical-White-Paper.pdf


If steering feedback is not comming the run main.cpp  and c which feedback id is being ued -- since its hardcoded right now to 2968 

