1. RPDO 1 Configuration (Command)Command: Write 0x1400 Sub 1 (RPDO1 COB-ID) $\rightarrow$ Value 0x80000201 (Disable)Response: Timed out ("Didn't receive SDO feedback")Result: Unknown (likely ignored or failed).
Command: Write 0x1600 Sub 0 (RPDO1 Mapping Count) $\rightarrow$ Value 0 (Disable Map)Response: ERROR 33554694Meaning: 0x06010002 = Attempt to write a read-only object.Conclusion: You cannot change the number of mapped items.
Command: Write 0x1600 Sub 1 (Map Slot 1) $\rightarrow$ Value 0x32180010 (Throttle)Response: ERROR 1090520070Meaning: 0x06040041 = Object cannot be mapped to the PDO.Conclusion: The controller rejects mapping this specific variable (or any variable) here.
Command: Write 0x1600 Sub 2 (Map Slot 2) $\rightarrow$ Value 0x32190010 (Brake)Response: ERROR 1090520070 (Object cannot be mapped).
Command: Write 0x1600 Sub 0 (Map Count) $\rightarrow$ Value 2Response: ERROR 33554694 (Read Only).
Command: Write 0x1400 Sub 1 (RPDO1 COB-ID) $\rightarrow$ Value 0x201 (Enable)Response: ERROR 33554694 (Read Only).Conclusion: You cannot change the COB-ID of RPDO1. It is fixed to 0x201 (default).

2. TPDO 1 Configuration (Feedback)Command: Write 0x1800 Sub 1 (TPDO1 COB-ID) $\rightarrow$ Value 0x80000181 (Disable)Response: Success (Accepted).Note: You successfully disabled TPDO1 transmission temporarily.
Command: Write 0x1A00 Sub 0 (TPDO1 Map Count) $\rightarrow$ Value 0Response: ERROR 33554694 (Read Only).Conclusion: Even though you disabled the PDO, the mapping table 0x1A00 is Permanently Read-Only in firmware.
Command: Write 0x1A00 Sub 1 through Sub 4 (Map Throttle, Brake, Speed, Accel)Response: ERROR 1090520070 (Object cannot be mapped) for ALL attempts.
Command: Write 0x1800 Sub 2 (Trans Type) $\rightarrow$ Value 0xFF (Async)Response: Success (Accepted).
Command: Write 0x1800 Sub 5 (Event Timer) $\rightarrow$ Value 50 (ms)Response: ERROR 518Meaning: 0x06020000 = Object does not exist in the object dictionary.Conclusion: TPDO1 does not support an Event Timer on this device.
Command: Write 0x1A00 Sub 0 (Enable Map) $\rightarrow$ Value 4Response: ERROR 33554694 (Read Only).

Command: Write 0x1800 Sub 1 (TPDO1 COB-ID) $\rightarrow$ Value 0x181 (Enable)Response: Success.3. TPDO 2 Configuration (Feedback)Command: Write 0x1801 Sub 1 (TPDO2 COB-ID) $\rightarrow$ Value 0x80000281 (Disable)Response: Success.
Command: Write 0x1A01 Sub 0 (Map Count) $\rightarrow$ Value 0Response: Success (Accepted!).Note: Unlike TPDO1, the controller allowed you to clear the count for TPDO2.
Command: Write 0x1A01 Sub 1 (Map RPM) $\rightarrow$ Value 0x32070010Response: ERROR 33554694 (Read Only).Conclusion: While it let you clear the count, it refused to let you add a new mapping. This is inconsistent behavior by the controller but the result is the same: Mapping Failed.

Command: Write 0x1A01 Sub 2, 4Response: ERROR 1090520070 (Cannot be mapped).Command: Write 0x1A01 Sub 3Response: Timed out.
Command: Write 0x1801 Sub 5 (Event Timer) $\rightarrow$ Value 50Response: ERROR 518 (Object does not exist).
Command: Write 0x1A01 Sub 0 (Enable Map)Response: ERROR 33554694 (Read Only).
Command: Write 0x1801 Sub 1 (Enable TPDO2) $\rightarrow$ Value 0x281Response: Success.Summary of ErrorsRead Only (0x06010002): The Mapping Objects (0x1600, 0x1A00, 0x1A01) are locked by the firmware. You cannot change what data is in the PDOs.Object Does Not Exist (0x06020000): The Event Timer (Sub-index 5) does not exist for these PDOs. You cannot set a frequency (e.g., 50ms) using this method.Cannot Be Mapped (0x06040041): The specific variables you tried to map are not allowed in the PDOs by the manufacturer.



RPDO 1 (Command You Send to Drive)
Byte 0: 0x33D1 (Byte 0) - Likely VCL_App_Var_1 (User Defined)
Byte 1: 0x33D1 (Byte 1)
Byte 2: 0x3218 (Byte 0) -> VCL_Throttle Low Byte
Byte 3: 0x3218 (Byte 1) -> VCL_Throttle High Byte
Byte 4: 0x304E (Byte 0) -> MotorTemp_Hot (?)


TPDO 1 (Feedback from Drive)
Byte 0: 0x33D3 (Byte 0) - Likely VCL_App_Var_3
Byte 1: 0x33D3 (Byte 1)
Byte 2: 0x321C -> PD_Current (Proportional Driver Current) 
Byte 3: 0x3226 -> Switch State (Bitmask of all switches) 
Byte 4: 0x3207 (Byte 0) -> Motor_RPM Low Byte 
Byte 5: 0x3207 (Byte 1) -> Motor_RPM High Byte
Byte 6: 0x3209 (Byte 0) -> Current_RMS Low Byte 
Byte 7: 0x3209 (Byte 1) -> Current_RMS High Byte

what are you trying to do? SDO Q is becoming large -- current and rpm feedback we will get 
so we can only take that --  send throttle also through PDO and read feedback through PDO
send brake through SDO   -- we cant read throttle feedback if its so - because in 1 loop controller can process only 1 SDO 